  "img": "modules/historia/Species/Storks.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><span class=\"fontstyle0\">In the eyes of many, the sight of black and white plumage, large wings and a bright orange beak is the symbol of salvation. Altruistic kind-hearted, patient and ready for action, the Storks were born to excel when the priority is helping others. There are countless companies of Stork nurses ready to fly when they receive the call, even when it comes from the battlefields. Although these Grarconi are not naturally dismissive of danger, the desire to lend their help is stronger than their fear. Luck often assists these generous souls, and many veterans or sick people who have now recovered will swear that touching the beak of a Stork is the best talisman: the Storks sigh, smile and endure, well aware that a hopeful sick person has more chance of recovering than one who has lost faith. Talkative, sunny and full of practical sense, Storks are welcome everywhere, but their tendency to “nurse” everyone can sometime create tensions with those who cannot tolerate being cared for as if they were a puppy or a sick person.</span> <br style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-size-adjust:auto\" /></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em><strong>Increase in Ability Scores.</strong></em> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Your <span class=\"fontstyle0\">Dexterity </span>score increases by 2 and your <span class=\"fontstyle0\">Wisdom </span>score increases by 1.<br /></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em><strong>Age.</strong></em> </span>A Grarconi reaches maturity around the age of 14 <span class=\"fontstyle0\">and is immediately considered independent. </span>They have an average lifespan of around 60 years.</p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em><strong>Speed. </strong></em></span></span>The base speed on the ground is 25 feet, and your <span class=\"fontstyle0\">flying speed is 30 feet.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em><strong>Size. </strong></em></span>A Stork can reach a height of between 4 1/4 feet and <span class=\"fontstyle0\">5 1/4 feet, and weigh between 65 lbs and 90 lbs.</span> <span class=\"fontstyle2\">Your size is Medium.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.ZLta2Wjm3OsgNAk0]{Wings}</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.DO8bJUsTURvkwDVu]{Pecking}</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.9ALHHLuQoSWQRqN4]{Prehensile Legs}</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.2zVRhhfSO8fMZWzt]{Acute Sight}</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.DNDaDMkNoAimSb3i]{Extended Flight}</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.Fr8OczGC9Gwhg4wM]{Lucky}</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">@Compendium[world.species-features.nC8uNKGFCwI6Azfa]{Sense of Care}</span></p>\n<p><em><strong><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Instinct of Familia, Aquatic (Predator): </span></strong></em><span class=\"fontstyle4\">“I am as fluid as the water I love so much”.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle4\"><span class=\"fontstyle0\"><em><strong>Instinct of Species, Pity:</strong></em> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">“I take care of the weak and the sick”.</span> <br style=\"font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;orphans:2;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-size-adjust:auto;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px\" /></span></p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
